FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:2481-2487 — Silent data loss on session restore: `parse_session_state` skips malformed macro records (unparseable line count at line 2481-2482, truncated body at lines 2486-2487) and malformed alias records (missing value at line 2474-2476) without any warning to the user. The comment at line 2465 acknowledges this ("skipped rather than panicking") but a user who manually edits their saved session file or experiences corruption would lose macros/aliases silently. No test covers this error path. VERIFIED: traced the exact code path in `parse_session_state` — `continue`/`break` discard data with no user-visible message.
2. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:702-705 — Unbounded resource use: `aliases: HashMap<String, String>` and `macros: HashMap<String, Vec<String>>` have no limits on entry count or macro line count. A user can define unlimited aliases or record macros with unlimited lines, causing unbounded memory growth. The REPORT.md claims "resource_limit — covered" but only cites cycle detection for aliases and "finite stored list" for macros — no actual bounds are enforced. VERIFIED: the struct fields at lines 702-705 are plain HashMaps with no capacity limits; no limit checks exist in `define_alias` (line 1248) or `start_macro` (line 1337).
3. [MINOR] src/repl/mod.rs:1320 — Unrecognized macro subcommand treated as macro name: the fallback `_ => self.run_macro(argument)` means `.macro statr foo` (typo for "start") attempts to run a macro named "statr foo" and reports "no macro named 'statr foo'" instead of a usage error for the unknown subcommand. No test covers this case.
4. [MINOR] src/repl/mod.rs:1187-1189 — Bare aliases (without sigil) cannot accept arguments after them: `expand_alias_line` returns `Ok(None)` when `!has_sigil && !rest.is_empty()`, so `ll extra` where `ll` aliases `:vars` is not expanded but `:ll extra` is. This asymmetry is not documented for users and could be surprising. No test covers this case.
5. [STYLE] tests/repl_test.rs:2006 and src/repl/mod.rs:4800 — Duplicate test name `edge_completion_offers_session_aliases_and_macro_names` across integration tests and module tests.

